# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Step 1. Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose a backend {#choose-a-backend}"
msgstr "Pumili ng backend {#choose-a-backend}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To detect errors during the circuit, we need to choose a backend that has access to the `MidCircuitMeasure` method (see the [documentation](/guides/execute-dynamic-circuits#mid-circuit-measurements)).\n"
msgstr "Para matukoy ang mga error sa panahon ng circuit, kailangan nating pumili ng backend na may access sa `MidCircuitMeasure` method (tingnan ang [dokumentasyon](/guides/execute-dynamic-circuits#mid-circuit-measurements)).\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build a sequence of bit-flip stabilizer circuits implementing multiple rounds of error detection and correction {#build-a-sequence-of-bit-flip-stabilizer-circuits-implementing-multiple-rounds-of-error-detection-and-correction}"
msgstr "Bumuo ng sequence ng bit-flip stabilizer circuits na nagpapatupad ng maraming round ng error detection at correction {#build-a-sequence-of-bit-flip-stabilizer-circuits-implementing-multiple-rounds-of-error-detection-and-correction}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The bit-flip code is among the simplest examples of a stabilizer code. It protects the state against a single bit-flip (X) error on any of the encoding qubits. Consider the action of bit-flip error $X$, which maps $|0\\rangle \\rightarrow |1\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle \\rightarrow |0\\rangle$ on any of our qubits, then we have $\\epsilon = \\{E_0, E_1, E_2 \\} = \\{IIX, IXI, XII\\}$. The code requires five qubits: three are used to encode the protected state (the \"data qubits\"), and the remaining two are used as stabilizer measurement ancillas.\n"
msgstr "Ang bit-flip code ay isa sa pinakasimpleng mga halimbawa ng stabilizer code. Pinoprotektahan nito ang estado laban sa isang bit-flip (X) error sa alinman sa mga encoding qubit. Isaalang-alang ang aksyon ng bit-flip error $X$, na nagmamapa ng $|0\\rangle \\rightarrow |1\\rangle$ at $|1\\rangle \\rightarrow |0\\rangle$ sa alinman sa ating mga qubit, kung gayon mayroon tayong $\\epsilon = \\{E_0, E_1, E_2 \\} = \\{IIX, IXI, XII\\}$. Ang code ay nangangailangan ng limang qubit: tatlo ang ginagamit upang i-encode ang protektadong estado (ang \"data qubits\"), at ang natitirang dalawa ay ginagamit bilang mga stabilizer measurement ancilla.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Below you will build circuits that (1) prepare the data qubits in the logical $|\\bar{1} \\rangle$ state, then (2) run multiple cycles of a $5 \\mu s$ delay followed by error correction (including reset of the syndrome qubits), and (3) read out the state of the data qubits.\n"
msgstr "Sa ibaba, bubuo ka ng mga circuit na (1) naghahanda sa data qubits sa logical $|\\bar{1} \\rangle$ state, pagkatapos ay (2) nagpapatakbo ng maraming cycle ng $5 \\mu s$ na delay na sinusundan ng error correction (kasama ang reset ng syndrome qubits), at (3) binabasa ang state ng data qubits.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will also test the lifetime of the $|1\\rangle$ state without using error correction by including three reference qubits that we prepare in the $|1\\rangle$ state, leave idle, and then read out.\n"
msgstr "Susubukan din natin ang lifetime ng $|1\\rangle$ state nang hindi gumagamit ng error correction sa pamamagitan ng pagsasama ng tatlong reference qubit na inihahanda natin sa $|1\\rangle$ state, iniiwan idle, at pagkatapos ay binabasa.\n"

