# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize the problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-the-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Step 2: Optimize the problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-the-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To reduce the total job execution time, Qiskit primitives only accept circuits and observables that conform to the instructions and connectivity supported by the target system (referred to as instruction set architecture (ISA) circuits and observables). [Learn more about transpilation](/guides/transpile).\n"
msgstr "Upang mabawasan ang kabuuang oras ng pagpapatupad ng trabaho, ang mga Qiskit primitive ay tumatanggap lamang ng mga circuit at observable na sumusunod sa mga tagubilin at koneksyon na sinusuportahan ng target system (tinutukoy bilang instruction set architecture (ISA) circuit at observable). [Matuto pa tungkol sa transpilation](/guides/transpile).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generate ISA circuits {#generate-isa-circuits}"
msgstr "Generate ISA circuits {#generate-isa-circuits}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will start by finding an initial layout (as in, a selection of physical qubits to map our circuits to) by transpiling the longest of our circuits using the preset pass manager with optimization level 3.\n"
msgstr "Magsisimula tayo sa paghahanap ng initial layout (ibig sabihin, isang pagpili ng physical qubits kung saan i-map ang ating mga circuit) sa pamamagitan ng pag-transpile ng pinakamahabang circuit natin gamit ang preset pass manager na may optimization level 3.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For the reference qubits that we will compare our logical quantum memory to, we will choose them to be the best available qubits in terms of amplitude damping coherence time ($T_1$).\n"
msgstr "Para sa reference qubits na ikukumpara natin sa ating logical quantum memory, pipiliin natin ang mga ito bilang pinakamahusay na available na qubit sa usapin ng amplitude damping coherence time ($T_1$).\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/repetition-codes/extracted-outputs/67acea4f-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/repetition-codes/extracted-outputs/67acea4f-0.avif)\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Step 3. Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Step 4: I-post-process at ibalik ang resulta sa nais na classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will now compare the error rates vs. time between the logical memory using the 3-qubit repetition code on the one hand, and the individual unencoded reference qubits on the other hand.\n"
msgstr "Ikukumpara na natin ngayon ang mga error rate laban sa oras sa pagitan ng logical memory gamit ang 3-qubit repetition code sa isang banda, at ang indibidwal na unencoded na reference qubits sa kabilang banda.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/repetition-codes/extracted-outputs/72ad282b-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/repetition-codes/extracted-outputs/72ad282b-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We clearly see an improved lifetime of the $|\\bar{1}\\rangle$ state, even compared to the best (unencoded) physical qubits. However, keep in mind that this experiment just corrects one type of error, namely bit-flips. Can you improve the lifetime of the logical qubit? You might want to explore optimizing the delay time, scaling up the size of the repetition code beyond $n=3$, etc.\n"
msgstr "Malinaw nating nakikita ang pinahusay na lifetime ng $|\\bar{1}\\rangle$ state, kahit ikumpara sa pinakamahusay na (unencoded) physical qubits. Gayunpaman, tandaan na ang eksperimentong ito ay itinatama lang ang isang uri ng error, ibig sabihin ang bit-flips. Kaya mo bang pahusayin ang lifetime ng logical qubit? Maaari mong tuklasin ang pag-optimize ng delay time, pagpapalaki ng sukat ng repetition code lampas sa $n=3$, at iba pa.\n"

